  "details": "Since WMR (Windows Mixed Reality) is much cheaper and it seems also very useful in VRChat use because you can pretty much except full body track.\nMore users will buy WMR as alternative for Oculus or Vive.\n\nBut default move is set on trackpad where you point new position and move forward.\nI don't like it, so i have changed settings in SteamVR to use joystick to move around.\nIt works good to move around, BUT... this also cause the SteamVR 'world' will move around. The original spot (the white area under you) will moved away from your position.\n\nIf i go spawn to world, sometimes i spawned outside the world area.\nRespawn will not help it, even trackpad move. With joystick i can walk back to world area.\nBut if i walk around again with joystick and choose for example another avatar from world, the chance is very high i spawned again outside or at edge of the world.\n\nIt seems VRChat cannot correct and hold last position before i change to another avatar.\nMove to another world is still very sensitive with joystick use. \n\nBut i must say, joystick move is much easier than trackpad move. I hope this can fixed for WMR users who want use joystick for move around.\n\nAnd with joysitck use, i saw also sometimes the trackpad move is rotated to 90 degrees right. This problem happens pretty much.\n\nBecause it's not nice if i spawn suddenly outside worlds and even inside world area i can even spawned to another spot, it's so akward problem.\n\nI have plenty video examples for this spawn problems.\n\nWhat can you do for WMR users?",
